title: The commands for your root note.
pid: a37f76bf-6a2d-405c-94a6-2c303c7c5703
body: |2-
  On waking: 'tools/team/pacer.sh holds'. Before writing anything:
  'tools/team/pacer.sh hold graph' (add 'code' when building, and each
  specialist's name before lending a mind to it); if it refuses, it
  says who holds what, and nothing was held. When done with something:
  'tools/team/pacer.sh release WHAT', or 'release' for everything. A
  session cut off lets go by itself. A session with Jeff that holds
  'graph' keeps the pacer waiting, as 'pause' did, until it releases or
  ends: so release 'graph' when you no longer need it, or the pacer
  waits as long as that Claude stays open.
